{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0301","billNumberShort":"H.B. 301","billNumberLong":"HB0301S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0170","shortTitle":"Drug Recodification","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"GWYNNM","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Gwynn, Matthew H.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCKELMK","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill technically reorganizes, revises, and clarifies provisions relating to drugs.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>technically reorganizes, revises, and clarifies provisions concerning drugs, including moving certain criminal offenses concerning drugs from Title 58, Occupations and Professions, into Title 76, Utah Criminal Code, and reorganizing remaining sections into organized structures; <hr><ltbullet>updates cross references; <hr><ltbullet>adds coordination clauses to:<hr><ltbullet1>coordinate changes between this bill and S.B. 117, Occupational and Professional Licensing Amendments, if both bills pass and become law; and<hr><ltbullet1>ensure the statutory numbering and renumbering made in this bill will be reflected in any new language added to the Utah Code by legislation that passes in the 2026 General Session and becomes law; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jackie Rogers","fiscalAnalyst":"Nate Osborne","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"OXSSRPFVFX","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-21 08:46:52.130","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel